Make PandaOmronKeyConverter.unmap_action tolerant of the action shapes our
policy actually emits.

Upstream indexes ``action.base_motion[..., 3:4]`` unconditionally and compares
``action.gripper_close`` / ``action.control_mode`` as bare scalars. Our policy
emits a 3-wide base_motion for embodiments without a torso DoF, and emits the
two mode flags as 1-element arrays, so upstream raises on the torso slice and
compares an array where a float is expected. Guard the slice and normalise the
flags through np.atleast_1d, returning np.array values so the dict stays
uniformly array-valued for the downstream robosuite call.

The sibling PandaPandaKeyConverter.unmap_action is deliberately left alone --
it is not reached by our eval paths and keeping it untouched keeps this patch
minimal against upstream.

diff --git a/robocasa/models/robots/__init__.py b/robocasa/models/robots/__init__.py
index 438ed7ea..2ed20ef7 100644
--- a/robocasa/models/robots/__init__.py
+++ b/robocasa/models/robots/__init__.py
@@ -473,10 +473,11 @@
     @classmethod
     def unmap_action(cls, input_action):
         output_action = type(input_action)()
+        base_motion = input_action["action.base_motion"]
         output_action = {
-            "robot0_right_gripper": -1.0
-            if input_action["action.gripper_close"] < 0.5
-            else 1.0,
+            "robot0_right_gripper": np.array([-1.0])
+            if np.atleast_1d(input_action["action.gripper_close"])[0] < 0.5
+            else np.array([1.0]),
             "robot0_right": np.concatenate(
                 (
                     input_action["action.end_effector_position"],
@@ -484,11 +485,11 @@
                 ),
                 axis=-1,
             ),
-            "robot0_base": input_action["action.base_motion"][..., 0:3],
-            "robot0_torso": input_action["action.base_motion"][..., 3:4],
-            "robot0_base_mode": -1.0
-            if input_action["action.control_mode"] < 0.5
-            else 1.0,
+            "robot0_base": base_motion[..., 0:3],
+            "robot0_torso": base_motion[..., 3:4] if base_motion.shape[-1] >= 4 else np.array([0.0]),
+            "robot0_base_mode": np.array([-1.0])
+            if np.atleast_1d(input_action["action.control_mode"])[0] < 0.5
